        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral leg pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "History of 6–8/12 of aching/heavy pain from thighs to calves, sometimes burning, increased over the last 4–6/52. Brought on by walking or standing; can walk approximately 50–100 m on flat ground before needing to stop. Relieved within 2–3 minutes by sitting or leaning forward. Exercise bike can be used for a long time with much less pain. Occasional foot tingling when pain is bad. No rest pain or nocturnal pain."
      }
    },
